PS5 HDMI: 4K120 as YCbCr 4:2:2 at 8 bits instead of RGB at 6 (v1.8.9, test)  [ps5-bazzite-deck]

amdgpu skips 6 bpc only for HDMI sinks and DP->HDMI dongles; the PS5's HDMI chip is a DP->HDMI
converter that doesn't report as one, so 4K120 left the GPU as RGB at 6 bpc (fits the DP link;
HDMI has no 6 bpc) instead of YCbCr 4:2:2 at 8 bpc, the format Sony's 4K120 setup for the chip
is made for. The PS5's HDMI connector now counts as the HDMI endpoint it is. Test for hsgodd's
GPU fault at 4K120 session switches (LG B4), which never happens at 4K60 or 1440p120.
The "over FRL" log line shows the format and depth that went out.
(The connector part is patches/parked/1.8-reverted/ps5-hdmi-no-6bpc.patch.)
---

--- a/drivers/ps5/hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/ps5/hdmi.c
@@ -1579,7 +1579,8 @@
 	atomic_inc(&frl_check_seq);
 	if (ps5_mode_frl(drm_match_cea_mode(mode))) {
 		setVideoAdditionalConfigFrlFlava3();
-		pr_info("hdmi: %dx%d@%d over FRL\n", mode->hdisplay, mode->vdisplay, drm_mode_vrefresh(mode));
+		pr_info("hdmi: %dx%d@%d over FRL (%s, %u bpc)\n", mode->hdisplay, mode->vdisplay,
+			drm_mode_vrefresh(mode), yuv422 ? "YCbCr 4:2:2" : "RGB", bpc);
 		mod_delayed_work(system_wq, &frl_check_work, msecs_to_jiffies(1500));
 	} else {
 		setVideoAdditionalConfigFlava3(mode);
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
@@ -2428,6 +2428,16 @@
 		     aconnector->dc_link->dpcd_caps.dongle_type ==
 			     DISPLAY_DONGLE_DP_HDMI_CONVERTER);
 	is_dp_or_hdmi = dc_is_hdmi_signal(signal) || dc_is_dp_signal(signal);
+#ifdef CONFIG_X86_PS5
+	/*
+	 * v1.8.4: the PS5's HDMI chip is a DP->HDMI converter, but doesn't report itself as a
+	 * dongle, so 4K120 went out as RGB at 6 bpc (fits the DP link; HDMI has no 6 bpc) instead
+	 * of YCbCr 4:2:2 at 8 bpc, which the chip's 4K120 setup (Sony's) is made for. On
+	 * hsgodd's LG that gave no picture. Treat it as the HDMI endpoint it is.
+	 */
+	if (ps5_dm_is_hdmi_connector(aconnector))
+		is_hdmi_ep = true;
+#endif
 
